## Why This Is Asked
This question tests practical knowledge in cross-account tenancy, ABAC, key management, PrivateLink, and incident response.

## Key Concepts
- ABAC in cross-account access with aws:PrincipalTag and aws:SourceAccount
- Lake Formation cross-account grants and data lake permissions
- Tenant-scoped KMS CMKs and rotation
- PrivateLink/Endpoint services for private connectivity
- Immutable audit trails with CloudTrail/Config
- 60-second breach containment via automated revocation and quarantine via EventBridge/Systems Manager
- Secrets rotation for service credentials

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example IAM policy snippet enabling GetObject only if requester's tag matches tenant
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": "s3:GetObject",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::tenant-bucket/*",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {
          "aws:PrincipalTag/tenant": "${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant}"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the 60-second containment workflow end-to-end?
- How would you monitor for misconfigurations that could bypass ABAC?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests real-time detection and automated containment of credential abuse in a multi-account CI/CD setup using OIDC tokens.

## Key Concepts
- OIDC-based cross-account access and trust policies
- Real-time threat detection: CloudTrail, Security Hub, IAM Access Analyzer
- Containment automation: credential rotation, trust policy adjustments, resource quarantine
- Automation tooling: EventBridge, Step Functions, Secrets Manager

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: IAM trust policy snippet with OIDC
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {"Federated": "arn:aws:iam::123456789012:oidc-provider/token.actions.githubusercontent.com"},
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {"token.actions.githubusercontent.com:sub": "repo:org/repo:ref:refs/heads/main"}
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the containment playbook?
- Which logs and metrics confirm rollback reliability and minimal pipeline disruption?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design cross-account enforcement, not just configuration. Evaluates orchestration of SCPs, KMS, bucket policies, VPC endpoints, and automated validation.

## Key Concepts
- Organization SCPs and service control scope
- IAM boundaries and cross-account KMS key policies
- S3 bucket policy with encryption/TLS requirements
- VPC Endpoints/PrivateLink hardening
- AWS Config rules, drift detection, automated remediation

## Code Example
```javascript
// AWS SDK v3 check example
import { S3Client, GetBucketEncryptionCommand } from "@aws-sdk/client-s3";
const client = new S3Client({ region: "us-east-1" });
async function checkEncryption(bucket) {
  try {
    const res = await client.send(new GetBucketEncryptionCommand({ Bucket: bucket }));
    console.log("Encryption:", res.ServerSideEncryptionConfiguration);
  } catch (err) {
    console.error("No encryption configured", err);
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
